#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Run TinyPilot with a disposable, visibly simulated device.

Usage: venv/bin/python3 dev-scripts/serve-webmcp-demo --port 8000

Uses the real Flask routes, authentication, CSRF, request parsers, SQLite
migrations, and Socket.IO input handlers. Each browser receives a private,
bounded in-memory micro desktop rendered as SVG—no VM, browser engine, subprocess,
or operating system is created per user. Typed text never executes. Power,
updates, accounts, Wi-Fi, hostname, diagnostics, and video preferences use
session-private sample state. At most 128 least-recently-used sessions are kept,
and all state is discarded on exit. This is not proof of physical hardware.

For an external bind, provide --username and set TINYPILOT_DEMO_PASSWORD (or
--password-env NAME). Use an HTTPS reverse proxy for browser WebMCP support.
The Flask debugger and reloader are always disabled, including external binds.
"""

